course: dictionary
lesson: 11505
title: Words for farming
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Agricultural is a long word, but you can work out its meaning from the words around it. It is an adjective, so it tells you about a noun, such as land, machines or a show. «The agricultural show had cows, sheep and huge pumpkins.» The show had animals and vegetables, so agricultural must have something to do with farming.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. «The farmer drove a big tractor across the agricultural land.» Tractors and land are both linked to farms, so agricultural means used for farming. Put in your meaning: "the farmer drove a big tractor across the farming land". It still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Agricultural is used a lot in geography and history. In geography, it describes land, jobs and regions used for farming. In history, it describes times when most people farmed. «Mia's dad studied at an agricultural college to learn how to run a farm.» The college teaches farming.
explain: Some phrases use agricultural often: agricultural land, agricultural show, agricultural college and agricultural machinery. If you meet a phrase you do not know, look at the main word after agricultural. Machinery means machines, so agricultural machinery means machines used for farming.
fact: Agricultural means to do with farming: growing crops and keeping animals.
fact: Agricultural is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as land, machines or a region.
fact: An agricultural region is mainly made up of farms.
fact: «Agricultural» can mean used for farming, as in «agricultural machines like tractors».
fact: Agricultural comes from the word agriculture, which means farming.
exercise: «The agricultural show had cows, sheep and huge pumpkins.» What does agricultural mean in this sentence? | To do with schools | Very large | *To do with farming | To do with the sea
exercise: Which of these is agricultural machinery? | A telephone | *A tractor | A bicycle | A kettle
exercise: «Mia's dad studied at an agricultural college to learn how to run a farm.» Find and copy the word that tells you the college is about farming. | college | studied | *agricultural | dad
test: Which phrase means a show where farmers display animals and produce? | science fair | sports day | fashion show | *agricultural show
test: Ella says an agricultural region is a busy city full of shops. What does agricultural region really mean? | *A region mainly made up of farms | A region covered by the sea | A busy city full of shops | A quiet town with no people
exam: In a history lesson, what does «agricultural» describe? | *Times when most people farmed | Times when there were no roads | Times when people lived in castles | Times when people lived at sea
